  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0. **Stacked on #1319** (#1313's swept cells, not yet on main): this branch is based on `issue/1313-midturn-swept-band`; its own change is the last commit.\n\n## What changed\n\nLaw (c3)'s overhang backstop - stock hidden under a ledge, which no column sample sees - still asked 4 path stations x 5 turn fractions per band, each at that pose's bottom plane. A holder or shank swinging through hidden stock between two of those poses got no `SweepHit` (#1316).\n\nIt now asks over the same reachable set #1313's column law reads, on its own coarser cells:\n\n- New module `crates/sim/src/verify/turn_hidden.rs`. Per live band, #1313's cells (hull of the column's two end discs, grown by the proven sag, swept along each tip chord) with the turn split so the sag is at most 0.05 mm (`BACKSTOP_SAG`, a tenth of the hidden law's 0.5 mm XY spacing), capped at 20 intervals (`BACKSTOP_PLANES`). The tip's chords are grouped into at most 4 runs, and at most `20 / intervals` of them.\n- One ask per (interval, run): at the lowest bottom any column of its cells reaches, over the union of their footprints. A point counts only where some position of a cell stands the band over it outside the flutes' kerf at that same tip position (`Cell::bottom_over`, unchanged).\n- New entry point `Rest::hidden_in_cover` in `hidden.rs`: the hidden region's boundary samples in the box, plus footprint probes (disc centres and rings at 5 tip positions per chord, built only when the plane has hidden stock near the box), filtered by that membership. A failed slice still convicts.\n- `turn_cells.rs`: `push_cells_with` (a stated sag budget and cap; `push_cells` keeps 0.001 mm / 64), `Cell::floor`, `Cell::probes`, `Cell::interval`. `sweep.rs` drops `backstop_columns`, `path_point` and the 4 x 5 grid.\n\n**Slice count per move:** at most 20 distinct planes per live band (`BACKSTOP_PLANES`), the same as the old 4 x 5 grid, so the slicing budget does not change. Pinned by the unit test `a_move_asks_at_most_twenty_planes_per_band`. Past the cap the cells only grow: a 90 degree turn at 150 mm reach overstates by 0.12 mm, still on the safe side.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `crates/sim/tests/midturn_hidden_backstop.rs` - `a_holder_crossing_hidden_stock_between_two_sampled_poses_is_convicted`: a holder 100 mm up the stack swings B 0 -> 80 under a ledge. At the old poses (20 and 40 degrees) its disc stands beside the hidden stock, and at 30 degrees it is inside it. Against the #1313 branch's `sweep.rs` it reports nothing (`[]`); here it reports `SweepHit { at: 0, part: false }`. Twins `the_same_swing_beside_a_bare_post_is_clean` and `a_swing_that_stops_short_of_the_hidden_stock_is_clean` stay clean.\n- Unit tests in `verify::turn_hidden`: the plane bound (straight and 50-chord ramps, turns from 1 to 120+ degrees, non-finite letters), and an ask covering the holder between its end poses.\n- `overhang_laws` (13) and `midturn_swept_band` (2) green, no assertion edited.\n- Quick gate `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on the final head: green - sim (25 suites incl. lib), motion (2) and app (47) gate-mapped suites, 75 binaries, 667 passed, 0 failed (7.4 min). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The release lanes (`--ignored`, the big posed fixtures) were not run, so false convictions and verify time on large real 5-axis programs near overhangs are not measured.\n- Pre-existing limits kept: one plane per ask (hidden stock the band meets above its bottom plane is not asked here), and the hidden region is sampled in XY by its own law.\n\nDecision note: `docs/decisions/1316-hidden-swept-backstop.md`.\n\nChangelog: Verify's mid-turn overhang backstop reads the whole turn instead of 4 x 5 sampled poses, so a holder or shank crossing stock hidden under a ledge between samples is reported\nEffort: high (not escalated)\n\nFixes #1316\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
